abstract: >-
  Exact small values for several problems from erdosproblems.com, with self-contained
  scripts. For problem #600, e(n,2) = 3T(n)+1 for n = 3..14, where T(n) is the maximum
  number of triangles in an n-vertex graph in which every edge lies in exactly one triangle.
  Computations were assisted by AI agents; all values were re-checked by an independent
  exact solver (see README, "Method and AI disclosure").
